References: comms/mail/mailroom/conductor/security__030-review-subagents-tools-allowlist.eml; team/conductor/reviews/; book.json TA1

Security found that review sub-agents briefed "read only" have reached for tools that act on a session, three times (an interrupt, a message, a session creation). The session's permission check denied every one, and nothing acted. Still, "read only" in a brief is a request, not a limit.

Three things, from now on:
1. The four review briefs in team/conductor/reviews/ now name the allowed tools (Read, Grep, Glob and Bash for reading) and say to report, never call, anything else. Use them as they stand.
2. If a step sub-agent of yours tries any other tool, record it in that wake's record, as the historian did.
3. Look back over your own wake records since 30 October for the same, and tell security what you find, so its register counts them all.

A tools allowlist for the review steps themselves (TA1) is with the editor.

